To repeatedly click a HTML element with the class "bdy" every second, you can use the following JavaScript code:

```javascript
setInterval(function() {
    document.querySelector('.bdy').click();
}, 1000);
```

This code uses the `setInterval` function to repeatedly execute an anonymous function every 1000 milliseconds (1 second). The `document.querySelector('.bdy')` method selects the first HTML element with the class "bdy", and the `click()` method simulates a click on that element.
